<%
  p = performance
  slug = { workspace_slug: current_workspace.slug }
  measured_roas = p.return_on_spend(:measured)
  recorded_roas = p.return_on_spend(:recorded)
%>

<section class="rounded-card border border-border bg-surface p-6">
  <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-normal">What it brought in</h2>
  <p class="mt-1 max-w-prose text-sm text-muted">
    Return on ad spend is the number most likely to make somebody spend more money, so it is
    only ever shown when both halves of it are genuinely known, and always with where the
    revenue figure came from.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <%#
      Source one: the platform. Only possible when a tracking tag on a website
      is telling it about purchases, which most shops taking orders on WhatsApp
      will never have.
    %>
    <div class="rounded-control border border-border bg-background p-5">
      <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-heading">Measured by the platform</h3>
        <%= render StatusBadgeComponent.new(
              label: p.measured_revenue ? "Tracked" : "Not tracked",
              tone: p.measured_revenue ? :success : :neutral) %>
      </div>

      <% if p.measured_revenue %>
        <p class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl tabular-nums text-heading">
          <%= MoneyPresenter.new(p.measured_revenue).full %>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
          from <%= number_with_delimiter(p.measured_conversions) %>
          tracked <%= "purchase".pluralize(p.measured_conversions) %>
        </p>

        <% if measured_roas %>
          <p class="mt-4 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-body">
            <span class="font-display text-2xl tabular-nums text-heading"><%= measured_roas %>&times;</span>
            <span class="ml-1">back for every rupee spent, by the platform's own count.</span>
          </p>
        <% end %>
      <% else %>
        <%#
          The explanation matters more than the empty figure. "No purchases"
          and "nothing was watching for purchases" are different statements
          about money, and only one of them is true here.
        %>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-body">
          No purchase value has been reported. That usually does not mean the ads sold
          nothing &mdash; it means nothing was measuring.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">
          A platform can only count a sale it can see: a tracking tag on a website, on a
          checkout that completes online. An order that arrives as a WhatsApp message or
          over the counter is invisible to it, whatever the ad did.
        </p>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <%#
      Source two: the shopkeeper's own till. For most Indian small businesses
      this is the only honest number available, and it is genuinely theirs.
    %>
    <div class="rounded-control border border-border bg-gold-tint p-5">
      <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-heading">What you counted</h3>
        <%= render StatusBadgeComponent.new(
              label: p.recorded_revenue || p.recorded_orders ? "Your figures" : "Nothing logged",
              tone: :neutral) %>
      </div>

      <% if p.recorded_revenue || p.recorded_orders %>
        <% if p.recorded_revenue %>
          <p class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl tabular-nums text-heading">
            <%= MoneyPresenter.new(p.recorded_revenue).full %>
          </p>
        <% end %>

        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
          <% if p.recorded_orders %>
            from <%= pluralize(p.recorded_orders, "order") %> you logged
          <% else %>
            recorded by you
          <% end %>
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4 space-y-1.5 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-body">
          <% if recorded_roas %>
            <p>
              <span class="font-display text-2xl tabular-nums text-heading"><%= recorded_roas %>&times;</span>
              <span class="ml-1">back for every rupee spent, by your own count.</span>
            </p>
          <% elsif p.recorded_orders && p.total_spend.nil? %>
            <p class="text-muted">
              No spend has been reported yet, so this cannot be turned into a return.
            </p>
          <% end %>

          <% if p.cost_per_order %>
            <p class="text-muted">
              <%= MoneyPresenter.new(p.cost_per_order).full %> of advertising per order.
            </p>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% else %>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-body">
          You know what these ads brought in and Prachar does not. Log the orders as they
          come and this becomes a real return on what you spent.
        </p>
      <% end %>

      <% if p.any_campaigns? %>
        <%= link_to "Record what came in",
              new_workspace_ad_campaign_outcome_path(**slug, ad_campaign_id: p.campaigns.first),
              class: "mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center rounded-control bg-primary px-4 text-sm font-medium text-primary-contrast hover:bg-primary-hover" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%#
    The rule, stated where both figures are visible. Two numbers of different
    provenance summed into one would be worth less than either.
  %>
  <% if p.measured_revenue && p.recorded_revenue %>
    <p class="mt-4 rounded-control border border-border bg-surface-sunk px-4 py-3 text-xs text-muted">
      These two are deliberately not added together. The platform's figure counts tracked
      online purchases; yours counts what actually came in. The same sale may well be in
      both, so a total would double-count it.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <% if p.outcomes.any? %>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-heading">What you have logged</h3>
      <ul class="mt-3 divide-y divide-border rounded-control border border-border">
        <% p.outcomes.first(8).each do |outcome| %>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-4 py-3">
            <span class="min-w-0">
              <span class="block text-sm text-heading">
                <%= outcome.occurred_on.strftime("%-d %b %Y") %>
                &middot; <%= outcome.ad_campaign.name %>
              </span>
              <% if outcome.note.present? %>
                <span class="block text-xs text-muted"><%= outcome.note %></span>
              <% end %>
            </span>
            <span class="shrink-0 text-sm tabular-nums text-body">
              <% if outcome.orders %><%= pluralize(outcome.orders, "order") %><% end %>
              <% if outcome.revenue %>
                <span class="ml-2 font-medium text-heading"><%= MoneyPresenter.new(outcome.revenue).full %></span>
              <% end %>
            </span>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</section>
